WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.134
-Hey, Colin.
How are you, buddy?

00:00:02.134 --> 00:00:03.402
-Hey, good.
How are you, Seth?

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.138
-[ Laughing ] Good.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.706
So, you are in Montauk
right now.

00:00:07.706 --> 00:00:11.177
This is the house
that you filmed your three

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.212
"Weekend Update" --
your quarantine editions

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:14.613
of "Weekend Update," correct?

00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:16.249
-That's correct, yes.

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:18.584
-Obviously, we both have friends

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:22.388
who are very kind
with their gifts.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:25.925
You sent me a photo of what
your co-anchor, Michael Che,

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:28.995
sent you for your birthday.
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:31.864
It was really a photo
I could only send

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:35.668
to fellow comedy writers.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:41.107
Michael Che
sent me a box on my birthday.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:44.710
And the card
that came with the box said,

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.413
"Dress for the job you want."

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:51.550
And then, I open the box,
and it was a police uniform,

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.586
a police officer's uniform

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:57.890
with a Republican National
Convention badge on it.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.760
And I opened it,
and I was like, "I don't --"

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.029
I laughed so hard
for like two minutes straight

00:01:04.029 --> 00:01:06.699
and then had no idea
what to do with it.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:09.168
And my friends were like,
"You should take one --

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:11.203
Might as well just take
one picture in it."

00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:13.773
I was like,
"That is the worst advice."

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.241
Like, "Oh, yeah,
what could go wrong

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.209
with one picture of you in it?"

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:19.345
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.881
-What I love the most about it
is a good amount

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.217
of thought and care
had to go into it.

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:25.451
-Oh, my God.
-He really went the extra mile.

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:28.021
-In the middle of a quarantine,
to track down

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:33.025
an official police uniform
and get it in the mail

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:36.496
to be delivered
by someone's birthday

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:39.098
when other people can't get,
like, toilet paper.

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:40.400
[ Laughs ]

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.004
-Colin, Che is
a huge friend to you.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.740
He is a great supporter of you.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.977
You are the person
who found him for "SNL,"

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.544
so you guys are really close.

00:01:52.544 --> 00:01:56.315
And yet he actively tries
to cancel you on social media.

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:59.518
This is a photo that he posted
on Instagram we have.

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:01.454
So, this is -- you guys
are hanging out together,

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.656
having a nice time.
-Yes.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.758
He came to visit me.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:08.761
It was very nice, and we got
to catch up and hang out.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.596
We were driving around.

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:12.665
And he, of course, noticed

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:16.769
that the local drugstore
is named "Whites."

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.172
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:23.510
And so he had me loop around
in front of it again

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:27.012
and then take a photo
of the two of us.

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:30.116
I was smiling in the photo.
He is grimacing.

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:31.750
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.054
And then, he wrote
that he made --

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.657
that I made him wait in the car

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:41.660
so that I could go into the
drugstore to buy TIKI torches.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:45.531
So I could go into Whites
drugstore to buy TIKI torches.

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:48.634
And then, the first comment
on the video is someone saying,

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:52.171
"I don't understand.
Are you guys friends or not?

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:53.639
Why would he do this?"

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.441
And Che immediately responds,

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.810
"We are not friends.
I think that's obvious."

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.845
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.281
And then,
everything he's been --

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.349
every post,
even if it's unrelated to me,

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:06.586
he's just been putting
#CancelJost.

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:07.954
[ Laughing ]

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:11.557
-And you are currently on
a press tour for your new book.

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:12.892
-Yeah.
-And this is a time

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:15.428
that I assume you have
a publicist working with you

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:16.962
to help you manage the press.

00:03:16.962 --> 00:03:18.564
What does your publicist
feel about

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:21.333
how your friend
is lending a helping hand?

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:23.970
-I would probably say
trepidation,

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:28.540
deep anxiety, confusion.
[ Laughing ]

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.310
-As a friend to you,
I was very happy --

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.779
And again, I think this is
anyone's goal in life

00:03:33.779 --> 00:03:35.547
is that your friends
will write a memoir

00:03:35.547 --> 00:03:37.416
and you will end up in it.

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:40.386
And there are multiple stories
about a trip that my brother,

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:44.957
Andy Samberg, and you took
to Scandinavia back in '07.

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:47.327
And I'm very glad that you --

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:49.095
I think a lot of people,
if this happened to them,

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.796
they would maybe leave it out
of their memoir,

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:52.565
but you are very honest
in this book,

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:55.001
and you do admit to the fact
that you fell asleep

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:56.936
in a graveyard
in Helsinki, Finland.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.470
-That's correct.
I come forward.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.639
I come clean on that.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:03.309
-My favorite detail about it is,
you know how bad I am

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.177
both with managing time

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:08.080
and understanding
the concept of time.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.951
And I remember
I fell asleep in what --

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:15.387
I took a nap on the way home,
walking home

00:04:15.387 --> 00:04:19.659
through Helsinki, Finland,
alone at 3:00 in the morning.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:23.795
I got tired, and I was like,
"I better take a power nap

00:04:23.795 --> 00:04:27.400
halfway through this city
I've never been in at night."

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.236
And I went into
what I thought was a park.

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:31.570
-Sure.
-And went into --

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.273
-So, of course, a great place
for a nap at 3:00 a.m.

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:39.478
Went into a park, fell asleep,
and then woke up

00:04:39.478 --> 00:04:41.580
what I thought was hours later,

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.216
and saw that
I was surrounded by tombstones,

00:04:44.216 --> 00:04:46.552
and that the park
was actually not a park

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:50.322
and more of an active cemetery.
-Yeah.

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:53.025
-And then, I came --
when I finally came back

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:55.861
and found you at the hotel
and woke you up,

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:57.463
I was like, "Oh, my God, Seth,

00:04:57.463 --> 00:05:00.098
I've been asleep
in a graveyard for hours.

00:05:00.098 --> 00:05:04.937
I must've been in there,
if not hours, maybe days even."

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:07.540
And you were like,
"Colin, it's been 45 minutes.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.475
We saw you 45 minutes ago
at a bar.

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:11.444
There's no way it was hours."

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:12.879
And that is my sense of time.

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:15.281
And then your brother,
very lovingly,

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.515
we were sharing a room.

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:20.819
He very lovingly saw
I was in a bad way,

00:05:20.819 --> 00:05:23.589
took all the pillows
from his bed,

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.291
sheets from his own bed,

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:28.861
made me a beautiful
makeshift bed

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:32.765
next to his own bed for me
to sleep on and rest.

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:35.735
And I, after he put
all that work in,

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:37.837
I fell asleep
directly next to him.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:40.373
-[ Laughing ]
-Not touching any of the blanket

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:42.607
or pillows
that he had set up lovingly

00:05:42.607 --> 00:05:44.443
and fell asleep on a hard

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.913
Helsinki wood floor
for the night.

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:48.981
-And I know people are thinking,

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:50.549
"Oh, you guys
are a little old for this."

00:05:50.549 --> 00:05:52.218
But this was a long time ago.

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:54.787
And when this happened,
I was in my mid 30s.

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:58.925
[ Both laugh ]

